=== QX001 | a query built by joining a value into its text, then run
q:{[s] value "select from t where sym=`",s}

=== QX001 | the value converted on the way in is still spliced
q:{[t] value "select from ",string t}

=== clean | a constant query has nothing spliced into it
q:{value "select from t"}

=== clean | value on a name says nothing about where the text came from
q:{[s] value s}

=== clean | a conditional choosing between constant queries splices no data
h:value $[a;"{select from x}";"{x}"],"y",b

=== QX001 | while a branch that is a value splices it (#653)
f:{[x;y] value "select from t where s=",$[x;y;"`a"]}
g:{[x;y] value "select from t where s=",$[x;"`a";y]}

=== clean | a string that is not a query
r:value "1+",string 2

=== QX002 | a password written into the source
password:"hunter2"

=== QX002 | under a namespace, any of the usual spellings
.cfg.apiKey:"abc123"

=== clean | a prompt is a message, not a secret
passwordPrompt:"Enter password"

=== clean | read from the environment, where it belongs
password:getenv`PASS

=== clean | an empty string holds nothing
token:""

=== clean | a literal that is only part of the value: a delimiter, a prefix
f:{[x] token:"," vs x; token}
g:{[x] token:"Bearer ",x; token}

=== clean | a lexer's tokens are syntax: punctuation, or a q word (#655)
sepToken:","
token:"if"
endToken:" ; "

=== QX002 | the whole value, before a comment or inside a lambda
apiKey:"abc123" / rotate yearly
f:{secret:"s3cr3t"; secret}

=== QX001 | get evaluates a string as value does (q 5)
f:{get "select from t where a=",x}

=== QX001 | and a handle hands it to the remote .z.pg
g:{[h;x] h "select from t where a=",x}

=== QX001 | so does a handle held in a namespace, the caller's .z.w, or the async neg form (#652)
f:{[h;s] neg[h] "select from t where s=",s}
g:{.conn.h "delete from t where s=",x}
k:{[h;x] (neg h) "update a:1 from t where s=",x}
l:{.z.w "select from t where s=",x}

=== clean | a constant query over a handle, and a joined string only shown
n:{[h] neg[h] "select from t"}
g:{[h] h "select from t"}
k:{show "select from t where a=",x}

=== clean | a lambda the file defines, applied to text, is a call and not a handle (q 5 prints the line, #345)
lg:{-1 x;}
n:5
lg "update finished for ",string n

=== clean | and so is one defined with :: (#654)
lg::{-1 x}
f:{lg "update finished for ",x}

=== clean | QX002: a column in an update or select phrase is not a variable - this one redacts it (#204)
r:update password:"***" from users
s:select user,password:"***" from users
f:{update token:"" from x}

=== clean | QX002: nor is a table-literal column, keyed or not (#204)
t:([]token:"ab")
u:([token:enlist "k"] a:enlist 1)

=== clean | QX002: an indented next line continues the value, which is then computed (#204)
password:"abc"
  ,x

=== clean | QX002: and so it does past a blank line (#675)
password:"abc"

  ,x

=== QX001 | the joined query in parentheses is the same query (#502)
f:{value ("select from t where s=`",x)}

=== clean | a parenthesised constant query (#502)
f:{value ("select from t")}
